<title>FRANCE: French overseas airports cargo down 2.5pct in '96.</title>
<headline>French overseas airports cargo down 2.5pct in '96.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's overseas airports handled 63,248 tonnes of global air cargo traffic in 1996, down 2.5 percent on 1995, figures issued by France's airports authority federation, UCCEGA, show.</p>
<p> Airports					 Pct change</p>
<p>						    on 1995</p>
<p> Bora-Bora (French Polynesia)     141   down 14.3pct</p>
<p> Cayenne (French Guyana)	  6,062   down  6.9</p>
<p>Fort-de-France</p>
<p> (French West Indies)	    13,485   down  0.5</p>
<p> Huahine (French Polynesia)	 108   up   11.0</p>
<p> Noumea  (New Caledonia)	  4,536   down  6.6</p>
<p>Point-a-Pitre</p>
<p> (French West Indies)	    13,473   down  3.5</p>
<p> Raiatea(French Polynesia)	  215   up    4.4</p>
<p> Reunion(Indian Ocean)	   18,074   down  0.3</p>
<p>Tahiti-Faa'a</p>
<p> (French Polynesia)		 7,154   down  3.5</p>
<p> Total				 63,248   down  2.5</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax:5017</p>
</text>
